<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ###########################################################################################
  TEMPORARY - DELETE THIS FILE (and the local-packages/ folder) WHEN benzene-dotnet PR #17 MERGES
  AND Benzene.Kafka.Streaming IS PUBLISHED TO NUGET.ORG.
  ###########################################################################################

  MarketDataAggregator depends on Benzene.Kafka.Streaming, the windowed/partitioned/checkpointed
  Kafka stream binding. It is real, reviewed, building code - benzene-dotnet PR #17, branch
  claude/kafka-stream-binding - but it has NOT merged to that repo's main and has NOT been released
  to nuget.org, so a normal restore cannot find it. Rather than write this service blind against an
  API nobody can install, the package is built from that branch into a local folder feed:

      git clone https://github.com/daniellepelley/Benzene.git /tmp/benzene-dotnet
      git -C /tmp/benzene-dotnet checkout claude/kafka-stream-binding
      dotnet pack /tmp/benzene-dotnet/src/Benzene.Kafka.Streaming/Benzene.Kafka.Streaming.csproj \
        -c Release -p:PackageVersion=0.0.2-alpha.4 \
        -o real-time-risk/dotnet/local-packages

  The folder is repo-relative (and gitignored) so the same path works on a developer machine, in CI,
  and inside the Docker build - NuGet resolves a relative source against this file's own directory,
  and the Dockerfiles copy the whole real-time-risk/dotnet folder into the build context.

  ONLY that one package is packed locally. Benzene.Kafka.Core is untouched on that branch and the
  branch point IS the 0.0.2-alpha.4 release commit, so every other Benzene.* package - including the
  Benzene.Kafka.Core this one depends on - still restores from the real nuget.org release, exactly
  like TradeLedger and RiskReadModels. That is also why the locally-packed version number is
  0.0.2-alpha.4: it is genuinely built from that release's source tree plus this one new project.

  WHEN THE REAL RELEASE GOES OUT:
    1. Bump every [0.0.2-alpha.4] pin in the .csproj files to the newly released version - the same
       one-line-per-package step the "Bump to Benzene 0.0.2-alpha.4" commit already did once.
    2. Delete this file, delete local-packages/ from .gitignore, and delete the "pack the unreleased
       Kafka streaming binding" step from .github/workflows/smoke-real-time-risk-dotnet.yml.
  Do not guess the future version number - read it off nuget.org once it exists.

  <clear/> is deliberate: it drops any machine- or user-level sources so a restore here resolves from
  exactly these two feeds. Nothing outside this folder is touched; no global NuGet config is modified.
-->
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" protocolVersion="3" />
    <add key="local-benzene-kafka-streaming" value="local-packages" />
  </packageSources>
</configuration>
